{title: 118 - The First Noel}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #118 • THE FIRST NOEL • 8.12.9.10}
{lyricist: Traditional English carol}
{composer: Wm. Sandy's Christmas Carols}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 118}
{meta: tune THE FIRST NOEL}
{meta: meter 8.12.9.10}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G7/F]The first [C/E]noel the angel [Am]did say
[G]Was [Am]to [C]certain [G]poor [C/G]shepherds [B7]in [C]fields [Am]where [G7/F]they [F]lay;
[C]In [G7]fields [C/G]where [G7/F]they lay [C/E]keeping their sheep,
[C]On a [Am]cold winter's [C/G]night [G]that was [Am]so [C]deep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Noel, Noel, [C/G]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born [F/C]is [G/D]the [F]King [C]of [G7]Israel
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G7/F]They looked [C/E]up and say [Am]a star
[G]Shining in the east, [B7]beyond [Am]them [G7/F]far,
[C]And [G7]to [C/G]the [G7/F]earth it [C/E]gave great light,
[C]And so [Am]it continued [C/G]both [G]day [Am]and [C]night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G7/F]And by [C/E]the light of [Em/B]that [Am]same star,
[G]Three [Am]wise [G]men came from [B7]country [G7/F]far,
[C]And [G7]to [C/G]the [G7/F]earth it [C/E]gave great light,
[C]And to [Am]follow the [C/G]star wherever [Am]it [C]went.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G7/F]This star [C/E]drew nigh to [Em/B]the [Am]northwest,
[G]O'er [Am]Bethlehem [G]it [B7]took [Am]its [G7/F]rest,
[C]And [G7]there [C/G]it [G7/F]did both [C/E]stop and stay,
[C]Right over [Am]the [C/G]place where [G]Jesus [C]lay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G7/F]Then entered [C/E]in those [Em/B]wise [Am]men three,
[G]Full [Am]reverently [G]upon [Am]the [G7/F]knee,
[C]And [G7]offered there, in [C/E]His presence,
[C]Their gold, [Am]and myrrh, [C/G]and [G]frankincense.
{end_of_verse}
